    - type: 0
      content: "Encountered invalid entry while reading serialization data for Unity
        object of type 'PlayerHeadFollower'. This likely means that Unity has filled
        Odin's stored serialization data with garbage, which can randomly happen
        after upgrading the Unity version of the project, or when otherwise doing
        things that have a lot of fragile interactions with the asset database. Locating
        the asset which causes this error log and causing it to reserialize (IE,
        modifying it and then causing it to be saved to disk) is likely to 'fix'
        the issue and make this message go away. Experience shows that this issue
        is particularly likely to occur on prefab instances, and if this is the case,
        the parent prefab is also under suspicion, and should be re-saved and re-imported.
        Note that DATA MAY HAVE BEEN LOST, and you should verify with your version
        control system (you're using one, right?!) that everything is alright, and
        if not, use it to rollback the asset to recover your data.\n\n\nA delayed
        error message containing the originating object's name, type and scene/asset
        path (if applicable) will be scheduled for logging on Unity's main thread.
        Search for \"DELAYED SERIALIZATION LOG\". This logging callback will also
        mark the object dirty if it is an asset, hopefully making the issue 'fix'
        itself. HOWEVER, THERE MAY STILL BE DATA LOSS.\n\n\nIF YOU HAVE CONSISTENT
